[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:40. Food and Talk]
[00:00.620]Passage 40 | 文章四十
[00:03.065]Food and talk. | 食物与谈话。
[00:06.980]Last week, at a dinner party, | 上周，在一个晚宴上，
[00:10.880]the hostess asked me to sit next to Mrs. Rumbold. | 女主人让我坐在伦博尔德夫人旁边。
[00:15.610]Mrs. Rumbold was a large, unsmiling lady | 伦博尔德夫人是一位身材高大、不苟言笑的女士，
[00:20.220]in a tight black dress. | 穿着一件紧身黑裙。
[00:22.885]She did not even look up | 她甚至没有抬头，
[00:25.085]when I took my seat beside her. | 当我坐在她旁边时。
[00:27.685]Her eyes were fixed on her plate, | 她的目光紧盯着自己的盘子，
[00:30.840]and in a short time she was busy eating. | 不一会儿她就忙着吃了。
[00:34.965]I tried to make conversation. | 我试图和她攀谈。
[00:38.920]"A new play is coming to the Globe soon," I said.| “一部新剧很快就要在环球剧院上演了，” 我说。
[00:44.940]"Will you be seeing it?" | “您会去看吗？”
[00:47.425]"No," she answered.| “不，” 她回答。
[00:50.830]"Will you be spending your holidays abroad this year?" I asked.| “您今年会在国外度假吗？” 我问。
[00:56.545]"No," she answered. | “不，” 她回答。
[00:59.575]"Will you be staying in England?" I asked. | “您会留在英国吗？” 我问。
[01:04.360]"No," she answered.| “不，她回答。
[01:07.360]In despair, I asked her whether she was enjoying her dinner. | 绝望中，我问她是否喜欢她的晚餐。
[01:13.480]"Young man," she answered,| “年轻人，” 她回答，
[01:16.680]"If you ate more and talked less, | “如果你多吃点，少说点，
[01:20.325]we would both enjoy our dinner." | 我们俩都会更享受晚餐的。”